Article 6 When trying theft cases, the circumstances of the crime of theft shall be determined based on the specific circumstances of the case:
(1) Where the theft of public or private property is close to the threshold for a "relatively large amount" and falls under any of the following circumstances, criminal liability may be investigated:
1. The theft causes loss of public or private property by destructive means;
2. The theft is of property of a disabled person, an elderly person living alone, or a person who has lost the ability to work;
3. The theft causes serious consequences or has other bad circumstances.
(2) Where the theft of public or private property has reached the threshold for a "relatively large amount" but the circumstances are minor and falls under any of the following circumstances, it may not be treated as a crime:
1. The perpetrator is a minor between 16 and 18 years of age;
2. All stolen goods have been returned and compensation paid;
3. The perpetrator voluntarily surrendered;
4. The perpetrator participated in the theft under duress and did not share the proceeds or obtained only a small amount;
5. Other circumstances are minor and cause little harm.
(3) Where the amount stolen has reached the threshold for a "relatively large amount" or a "huge amount" and falls under any of the following circumstances, it may be respectively classified as "other serious circumstances" or "other especially serious circumstances":
1. The principal culprit of a criminal group or the principal offender with serious circumstances in a joint crime;
2. Theft from a financial institution;
3. Theft by a roving criminal causing serious harm;
4. A recidivist;
5. Causing the victim's death, mental disorder, or other serious consequences;
6. Theft of materials for disaster relief, emergency rescue, flood control, special care for disabled servicemen and family members of revolutionary martyrs, poverty alleviation, immigration, relief, or medical treatment, causing serious consequences;
7. Theft of means of production, seriously affecting production;
8. Causing other major losses.
